WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.570
NARRATOR: The social
worker answers honestly.

2
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:10.820
She tells Tomás that the clinic does
not report to immigration and that what

3
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.150
he says stays in his record here.

4
00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.120
Then she names the limits: immediate
danger to himself or someone else,

5
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.830
abuse or neglect of a child or a
vulnerable adult, or a court order.

6
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:26.400
She adds that emergency help can
involve police or a hospital,

7
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.110
and that she cannot control what they do.

8
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:29.850
TOMÁS: Okay.

9
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:30.630
Okay.

10
00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.080
Nobody has ever said the
second part out loud.

11
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.100
Everybody just says "don't worry."

12
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.390
So I'll tell you about the danger
part, because you asked straight.

13
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.950
I'm not going to do anything.

14
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.050
I have my brother's kids on Sundays.

15
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:45.450
But three weeks ago I watched
a man die at the site.

16
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:47.190
Fell from the fourth floor.

17
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.850
I was the one holding him.

18
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.590
Nobody called anyone,
because of who we are.

19
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.890
That is what I see when I close my eyes.

20
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:55.600
Every night.

21
00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:57.580
I can't get it out of my head.

22
00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.040
If I tell you his name,
does that go anywhere?

23
00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.250
NARRATOR: Tomás has told you what he saw.

24
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:08.190
What has your honesty made possible,
and what must you ask next?
